60:# The two associativity cubes
61:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
63:# These are the whole trick.  For a table T of order n:
65:#   left_cube(T)[a, b, c]  = T[T[a, b], c]   -- (a * b) * c
66:#   right_cube(T)[a, b, c] = T[a, T[b, c]]   -- a * (b * c)
68:# gather_rows(T, flatten(T)) indexes T by every entry of T at once, producing
69:# the [n*n, n] matrix whose (a*n + b, c) cell is T[T[a, b], c].  Reshaping to
70:# [n, n, n] is the left cube.  The right cube is the same gather against the
71:# transpose, which yields axes in (b, c, a) order and is permuted back.
73:# All n^3 triples, no loop.
